{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And if it spreads.</b> It whitens the surface of the affliction like a blossom." "<b>From his head.</b> And not inside his head. <b>And to his feet</b> — and not inside his feet." "<b>For all the sight of the eyes of the priest.</b> Excludes a priest whose eyes' light has dimmed. And just as 'priest' excludes one whose eye's light has dimmed, so too 'day' excludes one [i.e., an inspection done] when the light of day has dimmed. Another interpretation: <b>for all the sight of the eyes of the priest</b> — excludes a place of concealment. From here they said: the man is seen as though hoeing and gathering olives, and the woman as though arranging [produce] and nursing her child."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:48.406508243Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}